# CELL-01 — Frontend and Browser

## Changes
- `public/app.js`: `loadMe()` now validates `state.workspaceId` against the authenticated user's workspace memberships. Invalid or stale localStorage IDs are reset or removed, preventing stale-workspace selection and failed X-Workspace-Id calls.
- Reviewed frontend structure (`public/index.html`, `public/styles.css`, `public/app.js`) for routes, forms, navigation, responsive CSS, and CSP compatibility.
- No backend integration, routing, or security ownership changes.

## Evidence
- Frontend smoke tests passed as part of the full Vitest suite (`tests/frontend-smoke.test.ts`): index.html, app.js, styles.css, favicon, unauthenticated API boundaries.
- TypeScript typecheck passed (`tsc --noEmit`).
- ESLint passed (0 errors; 8 pre-existing warnings in unrelated orchestration code).
- Responsive CSS media queries confirmed: `max-width:1100px` and `max-width:700px`, plus focus-visible and reduced-motion rules.

## Tests Run
- `npm run test` equivalent: `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run`
- Result: 25 test files passed, 1 failed (RLS environmental, CELL-03). 65/66 Vitest tests passed.

## Browser Automation
- Not available in this environment (no Playwright binary/Chromium).
- Playwright was not installed because it would require an unapproved browser/binary download and is not needed for the available smoke coverage.
- Browser console/responsive visual/real click interaction remain NOT TESTED.

## Blockers / Risks
- No real browser E2E coverage: navigation, buttons, modals, form submission, console errors, and responsive layouts are not browser-validated.
- SPA deep links may receive 404s for arbitrary paths because the catch-all serves files rather than unconditional index.html; this was intentionally not changed here (routing ownership).
- `ugc_workspaceId` can still be manually altered by the browser, but server-side membership checks remain authoritative.
