===== .mece/cells/CELL-02/REPORT.md =====
# CELL-02 — Ollama and API Integration

## Reproduction
- `/api/ollama/chat` was reproduced safely through the running local dev server.
- Request: `POST /api/ollama/chat {"prompt":"hi"}`
- Result: `402 Payment Required` with upstream Ollama Cloud message requesting usage credits or subscription.
- API key is configured server-side via `.env` (`OLLAMA_API_KEY` present, value not displayed). No secret value was printed.

## Determination
- The 402 is not a missing local application configuration or a model-name failure.
- Cause: Ollama Cloud account/plan lacks usable credits or subscription, therefore the upstream provider rejects the request.
- Required billing/subscription action is an external human decision and was not performed.

## Application Status
- `src/ollama.ts` reads `OLLAMA_API_KEY` only on the server; no browser exposure.
- `/api/ollama/chat` input validation and upstream status propagation are intact.
- Ollama remains intentionally outside `/api/integrations` provider registration because its credential is a shared server-side environment secret, not per-workspace browser configuration.
- No application-side defect was confirmed from the available evidence.

## Tests / Verification
- Existing integration tests passed.
- Typecheck and lint passed.
- Safe reproduction succeeded against local dev server with no write to upstream account.

## Blockers / Risks
- Real Ollama replies are blocked on external credits/subscription.
- Automatic callers receive an Ollama 402 error message through `OLLAMA_REQUEST_FAILED`; consumers should treat this as a payment-required condition.
- Model and endpoint health cannot be fully validated until credits are available.
